note as REVIEW_RULES_diagram_19_community
  TRUST & SAFETY RULES
  - CHECK overall_rating and dimension score between 1 and 5.
  - One active verified review per patient + target + completed encounter,
    unless an explicit repeat-review policy exists.
  - The public API exposes verified=true, never encounter_id.
  - Moderation, appeals, rate limits, abuse detection and immutable evidence
    are mandatory. Aggregate ratings exclude rejected/spam reviews.
end note

note as PHI_BOUNDARY_diagram_19_community
  PHI BOUNDARY
  Posts/comments/reviews must never contain identifiable patient health data.
  Consent is not used as a shortcut to publish PHI in the social domain.
  De-identified educational material requires a separate approved workflow,
  re-identification risk review and immutable moderation evidence.
end note

note as POLY_RULES_diagram_19_community
  OWNERSHIP INTEGRITY
  public_profiles.(target_type_concept_id,target_id) is restricted to approved
  practitioner, practice, site, hospital, diagnostic unit, pharmacy or approved
  organization types and validated against entity_registry. Specialized public
  projections expose verified services and current public prices, not internal
  contracts, stock cost, claim rules or clinical records. A comment has exactly one author identity: user or public
  profile. A review target is always one public profile.
end note

' ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' SOURCE CONSOLIDATED: diagram_19b_community_social_graph.puml
' ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
note as BIZ_diagram_19b_community_social_graph
  BUSINESS PURPOSE
  Brings the community layer up to the depth a real social platform requires, beyond
  simple posts and star reviews. Adds a generic, threaded commenting system usable on any
  commentable entity (posts, reviews, courses, groups), typed reactions, @mentions,
  hashtags and topics, interest/topic follows, groups/communities with membership and
  roles, shares/reposts and bookmarks, an addressable home/feed timeline with ranking
  inputs, and polls. Uses canonical generic comments, reactions and social_follows for posts,
  reviews, courses, groups, topics and profiles. PHI-free by design.
end note




