note as DEP_diagram_19b_community_social_graph
  Connects to other modules via:
  community (module 19) anchors (social_posts, public_profiles, post_comments,
  post_reactions, profile_follows), profiles.patient_profiles/health_practitioner_profiles
  (author_profile_id resolves to a public_profile), common.files (group cover), directory.tenants,
  terminology.catalog_concepts. Notifications for mentions/replies flow through messaging (35).
end note

note as PHI_BOUNDARY_diagram_19b_community_social_graph
  NO CLINICAL PHI in community. Comments, reactions, groups and feed are public/social
  content only. commentable/reactable targets are social objects; never patient records.
end note

note as REC_DERIVED_diagram_19b_community_social_graph
  REC 3.3 — DERIVED COUNTERS
  comments.reply_count/reaction_count, hashtags.usage_count, topics.follower_count,
  groups.member_count/post_count, polls.total_votes and poll_options.vote_count are DERIVED
  counters maintained by trigger. feed_items.rank_score is recomputed by the ranking pipeline.
end note

note as HARDENING_diagram_19b_community_social_graph
  REC 3.4 — HARDENING (enforce at DDL)
  - reactions: UNIQUE(actor_profile_id, reactable_type_concept_id, reactable_ref_id) (one reaction/actor/object; type is updatable).
  - poll_votes: UNIQUE(poll_id, poll_option_id, voter_profile_id); enforce single-choice when NOT allows_multiple.
  - group_members: UNIQUE(group_id, member_profile_id).
  - topic_follows / bookmarks: UNIQUE on (follower/profile, target).
  - content_hashtags: UNIQUE(hashtag_id, content_type_concept_id, content_ref_id).
  - comments: index (commentable_type_concept_id, commentable_ref_id, created_at);
    all polymorphic (*_type_concept_id,*_ref_id) -> value_set + trigger.
end note

note as VALUE_SETS_diagram_19b_community_social_graph
  VALUE SETS (bind *_concept_id; do not hardcode)
  commentable_type/reactable_type/bookmarkable_type->vs_social_object{post,comment,review,course,group,profile};
  reaction_type->vs_reaction_type{like,love,celebrate,support,insightful,curious};
  followable_type->vs_followable{topic,hashtag,group,profile};
  visibility->vs_group_visibility{public,private,secret};
  group_type->vs_group_type{community,professional,condition_support,practice};
  member_role->vs_group_member_role{owner,admin,moderator,member};
  join_status->vs_join_status{pending,active,banned,left};
  share_type->vs_share_type{repost,quote,external};
  item_type->vs_feed_item_type{post,share,comment,poll,recommendation};
  origin->vs_feed_origin{following,topic,group,suggested,promoted};
  status/state->vs_lifecycle_state.
end note

' ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' SOURCE CONSOLIDATED: diagram_19c_community_messaging_moderation.puml
' ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
note as BIZ_diagram_19c_community_messaging_moderation
  BUSINESS PURPOSE
  The interaction and trust-&-safety half of a real social platform: private direct
  messaging (1:1 and group conversations with receipts), an in-app social notification
  inbox, verified badges for professionals/organizations, user blocking, and a full
  moderation pipeline — queues, decisions, strikes and appeals — layered on the existing
  content_reports. Keeps social messaging strictly separate from clinical messaging
  (secure clinical comms remain in clinical/messaging). PHI-free.
end note




