note as DEP_diagram_19c_community_messaging_moderation
  Connects to other modules via:
  community (module 19) anchors (content_reports, public_profiles, social_posts, comments, reactions, social_follows),
  messaging.notification_requests (social_notifications.notification_request_id fan-out),
  identity_assurance (verified_badges evidence), common.files (attachments),
  directory.tenants, terminology.catalog_concepts.
end note

note as DRIFT_conversation_participants_F44
  DRIFT CLOSED (2026-09-11)
  is_favorite, is_pinned and archived_at (F4.4 · per-participant inbox state)
  existed ONLY in the MikroORM entity: neither this diagram nor SQL/19_community
  declared them, so a stack rebuilt from the model did not have them and every
  ORM write against those columns would fail. Declared here so the model is the
  source again. Types and nullability are exactly the ones the entity already
  used; no product decision was taken.
end note

note as RULES_chat_auto_replies
  CHAT AUTO-REPLY (F4.7)
  chat_auto_replies holds ONE row per public profile (ux_chat_auto_replies_public_profile_id):
  it is a preference of the person, not of a conversation. The column is named
  public_profile_id so the FK convention resolves it on its own: the generator
  pluralises the prefix and finds community.public_profiles.

  Server-side rule, evaluated on every INCOMING message:
    reply IF is_active
       AND the recipient has been idle for >= inactivity_minutes
       AND that conversation was not auto-replied within the last cooldown_hours
       AND (NOT only_outside_business_hours OR now is outside [from, to]).

  conversation_participants.last_auto_reply_at is the cooldown mark: it lives on the
  participant row of WHO REPLIES, which is exactly one row per (conversation, profile).
  A separate log table would say the same thing with a join.

  business_hours_from > business_hours_to is legal and means the range crosses
  midnight — the night shift. Both are NULL when only_outside_business_hours is false.

  The auto-reply is a NORMAL direct_message sent by the profile: it is not a
  different kind of message, and the other side must be able to reply to it.
end note

note as PHI_BOUNDARY_diagram_19c_community_messaging_moderation
  SOCIAL, NOT CLINICAL. Direct messaging here is social/consumer messaging. Secure clinical
  communication and patient notifications stay in clinical/messaging. No PHI in DMs, moderation
  records or notifications.
end note

note as REC_DERIVED_diagram_19c_community_messaging_moderation
  REC 3.3 — DERIVED
  conversations.message_count/last_message_at and moderation_strikes point totals are DERIVED
  (trigger). message_receipts is append-only; read state derives from the latest receipt.
end note

note as HARDENING_diagram_19c_community_messaging_moderation
  REC 3.4 — HARDENING (enforce at DDL)
  - conversation_participants: UNIQUE(conversation_id, participant_profile_id).
  - user_blocks: UNIQUE(blocker_profile_id, blocked_profile_id); CHECK blocker <> blocked.
  - verified_badges: partial UNIQUE(subject_type_concept_id, subject_ref_id, badge_type_concept_id) WHERE status='active'.
  - message_receipts: append-only; PARTITION BY recorded_at; UNIQUE(direct_message_id, recipient_profile_id, receipt_type_concept_id).
  - moderation_appeals: one open appeal per decision (partial UNIQUE WHERE status='open').
  - polymorphic (*_type_concept_id,*_ref_id) -> value_set + trigger.
end note

note as VALUE_SETS_diagram_19c_community_messaging_moderation
  VALUE SETS (bind *_concept_id; do not hardcode)
  conversation_type->vs_conversation_type{direct,group};
  participant role->vs_conv_role{owner,admin,member};
  content_type(dm)->vs_dm_content{text,image,file,voice,system};
  receipt_type->vs_receipt_type{delivered,read};
  notification_type->vs_social_notification{follow,mention,reply,reaction,share,group_invite,badge};
  source_type->vs_social_object{post,comment,review,course,group,profile};
  badge_type->vs_badge_type{verified_professional,verified_organization,top_contributor};
  verification_method->vs_verification_method{credential,manual,domain,document};
  moderation content_type->vs_moderatable{post,comment,review,message,profile,group};
  moderation source->vs_moderation_source{user_report,ml_filter,proactive,appeal};
  decision->vs_moderation_decision{approved,removed,restricted,warned,escalated};
  action_taken->vs_moderation_action{none,remove_content,mute,suspend,ban,shadow_limit};
  strike severity->vs_strike_severity{minor,major,severe};
  appeal resolution->vs_appeal_resolution{upheld,overturned,partial};
  status/state->vs_lifecycle_state.
end note

